                <pb facs="0746" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">551.5F1/190: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-16T16:00:00+00:00">December 16, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—12:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>462. As soon as I returned from Paris I consulted with the Foreign Secretary, Sir
                    John Simon, on the issue referred to in the Department’s 331, November 19, 4
                    p.m. Sir John assured me that the proposal would be discussed in the Cabinet,
                    and that subsequently I would be informed. In turn, I shall cable the
                    Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
